# Sessions live in the sidebar; new session stays discoverable

id: desktop-session-navigation
version: 1
status: proposed
title: Session-only sidebar navigation

goal: >
  Users pick and manage sessions from the collapsible left sidebar. The top bar
  handles repo scope only. New sessions must remain obvious without crowding the
  top bar.

recommendation:
  primary: sidebar
  secondary_optional: session_dropdown_in_top_bar
  rationale: >
    Session lists are longer and benefit from scroll, search, status dots, and
    context menus already in VirtualSessionList. A second top-bar dropdown
    duplicates the sidebar unless the sidebar stays collapsed by default.

regions:
  session_sidebar:
    scope: active_repo_only
    sections:
      - header:
          - label: Sessions
          - actions: [new_session, search_optional]
      - body:
          - virtualized_session_list
          - row: title, status dot, delete on hover
      - footer:
          - settings_link
          - theme_toggle_optional_relocate

flows:
  - name: select_session
    trigger: click_session_row_in_sidebar
    steps:
      - goto /workspace
      - desktopState.handleSwitchSession(sessionPath, repoPath)
    outcome: transcript loads; composer focused per existing shortcuts

  - name: new_session_from_sidebar
    trigger: click_new_session_in_sidebar_header
    steps:
      - desktopState.enterLanding with active repoPath
      - goto /
    outcome: SessionLanding with repo preselected; user submits prompt to start

  - name: new_session_keyboard
    trigger: Cmd+N
    steps:
      - same as new_session_from_sidebar when repoPath set
      - else focus landing composer on /
    outcome: unchanged from current global shortcut behavior

  - name: sidebar_collapsed
    trigger: user_closes_sidebar_or_offcanvas
    steps:
      - session list hidden
      - top bar repo dropdown still switches repo
      - user reopens via toggle or Cmd+B
    outcome: full width for workspace; session pick requires opening sidebar

alternative_considered:
  id: session_dropdown_in_top_bar
  placement: right_of_repo_dropdown
  pros:
    - switch session without opening sidebar
    - pairs with always-collapsed sidebar for maximum space
  cons:
    - poor fit for long lists and virtualized rows
    - duplicates VirtualSessionList logic
    - crowded top bar on narrow windows
  verdict: defer unless user testing shows sidebar-open rate is too low

flows_new_session:
  recommended:
    - location: sidebar_header_primary_button
    - label: New session
    - shortcut: Cmd+N
  acceptable_secondary:
    - command_menu: New session
    - landing_route: / when no session selected

empty_states:
  - no_sessions_in_repo:
      sidebar: No sessions yet + New session
      workspace: empty transcript prompt
  - no_session_selected:
      workspace: Choose a session from the sidebar
  - sidebar_closed_no_selection:
      workspace: Open sidebar to pick a session or use Cmd+N

acceptance:
  - All session rows for active repo visible in sidebar only
  - New session reachable in one click from expanded sidebar
  - No repo folders in sidebar (repo switch only via top bar)
  - VirtualSessionList and session delete flows preserved

implementation_notes:
  map_to_files:
    - AppSidebar.svelte — remove repo accordion; session list only
    - new AppTopBar.svelte — toggle + RepoDropdown
    - +layout.svelte — Sidebar.Provider wraps body below top bar, not full screen
    - PageShell / AppHeader — merge or remove duplicate Sidebar.Trigger
  state:
    - repos still in desktopState.repos for dropdown data
    - expand/collapse per-repo in sidebar may become unnecessary

open_questions:
  - id: cross_repo_session_memory
    question: When returning to a repo, restore last selected session?
  - id: search
    question: Keep command menu (Cmd+K) as primary session search vs sidebar filter?
